//   * each lane streams one uint32 = 4 E4M3FN codes per 128-wide scale
//     segment (fully coalesced 128 B per warp per segment), decodes with
//     bit assembly (normals) or a small LUT (subnormals), and accumulates
//     in fp32; one warp shuffle reduction and one round-to-nearest-even
//     bfloat16 store per row.
// The op is memory-bound on the weight bytes at M=1 (AI ~ 2 FLOP/byte):
// no dequantized buffer is ever materialized.
